  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Saga order in TransferOrchestrationService",
      "items": [
        "1. Idempotency: a repeated key replays the cached response; a concurrent duplicate gets 409. 2. KYC limits via account-service, fail closed; the lock token is released in the finally block.",
        "3. Risk: BLOCK returns 403; ADVISORY_WARNING needs the scam advisory acknowledged. 4. Biometric step-up for high value or risk score 60+. 5. Cool-off hold of 10 minutes for PHP 250,000 and above.",
        "6. Post to CBS as OFS (EP1). Interbank transfers first debit the sender into the Nostro account through CBS Client, then send the wire; a failed wire runs the compensating reversal (EP2)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Resilience and cache use",
      "items": [
        "CbsClientService wraps posting in Resilience4j retry and circuit breaker. When CBS or its database is down it publishes a failed-transfer event to the banking.transfers.dlq Kafka topic and tells the customer no money moved. Limit-check outages are queued to the DLQ too.",
        "Redis holds the idempotency lock and cached response, the 5 minute biometric challenge with its attempt counter, and the cool-off payload. Only the first is drawn as an arrow."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Other controllers in this container",
      "items": [
        "ReversalOrchestratorController (/api/v1/reversals: request, approve, reject, direct) calls CBS EP2 /reversal through its own WebClient.",
        "InterbankIngressController (/api/v1/interbank/transfers/inward) credits the local beneficiary through CbsClientService. The same class hosts the mock partner used when PARTNER_BANK_URL is not overridden.",
        "InterbankDirectoryController lists active participant banks from BankRoutingService, which refreshes them from CBS."
      ]
    }
  ]
